experiment: duty
  instrument        duty   trial seed 000000000139fd84   428 trials per arm
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  duty -- can the creature be POWER-GATED between words? `cost` puts its
  9.054e5 ops/s at 293x-276,000x BELOW a chip's 250-500 mW active floor, so
  operations are not the power bill -- being AWAKE is, and it currently runs
  awake 100% of the time.
  gating       FROZEN: neither ear nor step is called, so no state decays and
               no internal time passes. The world is still rendered every
               tick, so the acoustics are identical across arms.
  the risk     DERIVED, not guessed: the index is an EMA with a 1000-tick
               time constant. Awake, 1100 ticks of post-reward silence decay
               it to exp(-1.1) = 33%; FROZEN it decays to 100%. So a gated
               creature should carry the PREVIOUS word into the next one.
  the stat     ctxaxis's: per-BIT held-out accuracy, slot-to-bit map fitted
               on the training half only, so chance is exactly 0.50.
  18 creatures, 3 arms, 4 slots.

  arm          n   duty     present   bit F1           bit F2
  awake         18  1.000    1.000     0.913 +/- 0.031    0.755 +/- 0.027
  gated         18  0.607    1.000     0.902 +/- 0.021    0.846 +/- 0.033
  gated-long    18  0.304    1.000     0.902 +/- 0.021    0.846 +/- 0.033

  THE PRIMARY, paired per creature against `awake`:
    gated        bit F1  -0.011 +/- 0.040 (-0.3 SE)
    gated        bit F2  +0.091 +/- 0.030 (3.0 SE)   RESOLVED GAIN
    gated-long   bit F1  -0.011 +/- 0.040 (-0.3 SE)
    gated-long   bit F2  +0.091 +/- 0.030 (3.0 SE)   RESOLVED GAIN

  FREEZE CHECK: `gated-long` minus `gated` = 0 / 0 on the two bits.  EXACT, as it must be:
    a frozen creature cannot tell how long it was off, so the two arms see
    the IDENTICAL awake ticks and only the duty denominator differs. The gate holds.

  POWER-GATING IS FREE, and the derived prediction is REFUSED: freezing
  between words does NOT degrade the index, so the EMA's failure to decay
  across the gap does not smear it. **And because the freeze is EXACT the
  result is SCALE-FREE in the gap**: a creature that pays nothing at a duty
  of 0.304 pays nothing at ANY sparsity, because the awake ticks are
  identical either way. So the deployment win is set by how often words
  arrive and not by anything in the creature -- a word every 10 s is ~17%
  duty, a word a minute ~2.8%. That is a larger factor than the whole trim
  bought, from a mechanism the creature already has.

  WHAT THIS DOES NOT SHOW: that NAMING survives gating. This measures the
  INDEX, which is the mechanism the freeze threatens and the cheap half of
  the question. A naming run is ctxgrid-scale (4-5 h) and is only worth
  spending once the index is known to survive.
